<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Miss Wheatley returns two weeks after her first visit. This morning she had spirometry before and after albuterol and FeNO in the pulmonary function laboratory, and she then saw Dr. Fairbanks-Mensah. Her symptoms are unchanged in the cold weather: wheeze and cough on three or four days a week, waking with a tight chest about twice a month, and breathlessness climbing hills in the wind. The tuberculosis blood test and urine pregnancy test from the first visit were negative. She wants to understand exactly what the tests show and asks whether she will be well enough to travel by sea later in the spring. She came alone and was seen alone. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tests this morning</td><td>Spirometry with bronchodilator response, and FeNO</td></tr><tr><td>Results from the first visit</td><td>Interferon-gamma release assay negative; urine pregnancy test negative; chest X-ray clear; blood eosinophils 0.38</td></tr><tr><td>Her question</td><td>Is it asthma, and can she travel by sea in the spring?</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

