<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Asthma, confirmed, mild persistent (J45.30)</content>. Asthma confirmed: FEV1/FVC 0.72 is below the lower limit of normal for her age and rises to 0.80 after albuterol, with a 330 mL (15 percent) rise in FEV1; FeNO 38 ppb and blood eosinophils of 0.38 point to type 2 inflammation, and she is sensitized to house dust mite. Tuberculosis and other chest disease are excluded by a negative interferon-gamma release assay and a clear chest X-ray. Read with race-neutral equations, her FEV1 is 83 percent of predicted. Symptoms on several days a week but fewer than daily, with waking twice a month, fit GINA step 2. [S]<list><item>Budesonide-formoterol 160/4.5 mcg, one inhalation as needed for symptoms and before going out in the cold, up to 12 a day (GINA track 1, step 2); no albuterol-only reliever.</item><item>Inhaler technique taught with a spacer and checked today.</item><item>Written asthma action plan; peak flow meter and a two-week diary to set her personal best.</item><item>Influenza, COVID-19 and pneumococcal (PCV20) vaccines today.</item><item>Triggers: open a window and use a fan when cooking, keep away from fireplace smoke, a scarf over the mouth in cold wind, mite-proof bedding covers.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Wheeze, cough and breathlessness (R06.2)</content>. Explained by the diagnosis made today; superseded. [S]<list><item>Problem resolved.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Spirometry with bronchodilator response, read with race-neutral equations</td><td>At diagnosis, before starting controller therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>FEV1 2.24 L (83 percent) to 2.57 L (+330 mL, +15 percent); FEV1/FVC 0.72 to 0.80</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>FeNO</td><td>When the diagnosis is uncertain, and to monitor response (NAEPP, conditional)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>38 ppb, intermediate</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Blood eosinophils and total and specific IgE (phenotyping)</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Eosinophils 0.38 two weeks ago; total IgE 165; house dust mite specific IgE positive; cat and mold negative</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Exclusion of tuberculosis and other chest disease</td><td>At diagnosis, for a person born where tuberculosis is common</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Interferon-gamma release assay negative and chest X-ray clear at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Asthma Control Test, symptoms, night waking and reliever use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Asthma Control Test 16; symptoms three or four days a week; night waking twice a month</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique with her own inhaler, and adherence</td><td>Every visit; before any step-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taught today with her new inhaler and a spacer; demonstrated correctly</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Written asthma action plan</td><td>Every visit and after every exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Written plan with peak flow zones given</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exacerbation history (oral corticosteroid courses, emergency visits, admissions)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No oral corticosteroid course, emergency visit or admission ever</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Step-up or step-down assessment (GINA track 1)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Starting at step 2: as-needed low-dose budesonide-formoterol</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Triggers, exposures and smoking or vaping</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked or vaped; cold air, cooking and fireplace smoke, colds; house dust mite sensitization</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Comorbidities: rhinitis, reflux, mood, anxiety</td><td>At diagnosis and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No rhinitis or reflux symptoms; PHQ-2 1 at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccinations</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Influenza, COVID-19 and PCV20 today</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Biologic assessment</td><td>When asthma is severe or uncontrolled despite optimized step 4 to 5 treatment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Mild asthma; treatment has only now started</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Equity: race-neutral interpretation and plain explanation</td><td>Every test</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Read with GLI Global equations; results explained to her in plain words, with a printed copy for her</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Private conversation: consent, safety and exploitation, and her own decisions</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen alone; she consented to each test and treatment; results kept to her own contact details</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A confirmed diagnosis within two weeks: spirometry with bronchodilator response and FeNO, with tuberculosis excluded. Outcome by 1773-02-23: Asthma confirmed by a 330 mL (15 percent) bronchodilator response and FeNO 38 ppb; tuberculosis test negative and chest X-ray clear, two weeks after the first visit [S]</item><item>Asthma Control Test 20 or more with no night waking. In progress; target 1773-04-06 [S]</item><item>Correct inhaler technique and a written action plan she can use at home and at sea. In progress; target 1773-04-06 [S]</item><item>Well enough to make the sea journey and spend the summer away. In progress; target 1773-09-21 [S]</item><item>No exacerbation needing an oral corticosteroid. In progress; target 1773-10-26 [S]</item><item>Hepatitis B and HPV vaccination complete. In progress; target 1774-01-25 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, this season; COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, this season&apos;s formula; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026); Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); Bhakta NR, et al. Race and Ethnicity in Pulmonary Function Test Interpretation: An Official American Thoracic Society Statement. Am J Respir Crit Care Med 2023;207(8):978-995 (PMID 36973004) (2023); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-week review. Follow the action plan: more reliever inhalations and a call to the clinic in the yellow zone; emergency care in the red zone. Next scheduled visit 1773-04-06: six-week asthma review: control, technique, personal best peak flow, triggers, and planning for a long sea journey and a summer away. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
